<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
    Android Auto Backup, API 31 and above. backup_rules.xml is the same set for API 30 and below —
    see the reasoning there, which is not repeated.

    The two scopes differ on purpose:

    - cloud-backup is the Google-account upload the privacy policy names, and the ~25 MB all-or-
      nothing quota ADR-0005 is written against. The gallery stays out of it.

    - device-transfer is a direct phone-to-phone copy when the owner moves to a new device. No cloud
      account is involved, so the policy's promise does not cover it, and there is no quota, so
      ADR-0005's reason for excluding photos does not apply either. Silently dropping a bunny's
      whole gallery on a phone upgrade would be the worse failure, so photos ride along.

    preserved/ is excluded from both: an unbounded, never-pruned scratch directory is not something
    to carry onto a new phone unasked (ADR-0007).
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="file" path="photos/" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="preserved/" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="file" path="preserved/" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
